{"v":1,"accession":"PRJNA1078539","title":"Distinct microbial communities enriched in water-saturated and unsaturated reactors influence the performance of integrated Hydroponics-Microbial Electrochemical Technology","description":"The goal is to understand the microbial communities involved in the wastewater treatment andelectricity generation performance of the integrated Hydroponics-Microbial ElectrochemicalTechnology (iHydroMET), which is an emerging decentralized domestic wastewatermanagement solution for point sources. After 4 months of system operation with clarifiedsewage, the microbial communities enriched in different zones of the reactors of iHydroMETsystem operated in water-saturated (i.e., water-logged) and unsaturated (i.e., free-drained)conditions were assessed. Samples were taken from five places of both conditions, which areanodic (Graphite + granular activated carbon) zone, bottom cocopeat, top cocopeat, cathodicgraphite, and influent sewage.","center":"Indian Institute of Science Education and Research Mohali","data_type":"Raw sequence reads","submission_date":"2024/02/21 00:00","sample_cols":["accession","title","tier","context","collection_date","collection_year","country","region","place_id","place","location_status","lat","lon","submitted_location","isolation_source","env_broad_scale","env_local_scale","env_medium","eligibility_reason"],"samples":[["SAMN40005178","Anodic zone of water-unsaturated reactor","uncertain",null,"2021-06-10",2021,"IN","Chandigarh",1274746,"Chandigarh","probable",30.665,76.73,"India: IISER Mohali, Punjab","iHydroMET reactor",null,null,null,"environmental sample; urban association not established"],["SAMN40005179","Bottom cocopeat of water-unsaturated reactor","uncertain",null,"2021-06-10",2021,"IN","Chandigarh",1274746,"Chandigarh","probable",30.665,76.73,"India: IISER Mohali, Punjab","iHydroMET reactor",null,null,null,"environmental sample; urban association not established"],["SAMN40005180","Top cocopeat of water-un